    "sourceUrl": "https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf",
    "note": "720 W across the 8 PoE++ ports: exactly 8 x 90 W, so this is the M4250 where the budget and the port maxima meet - every port can carry an Ultra90 90 W load at once. Single fixed C14 inlet (no second PSU)."
  },
  "notes": "M4250 series common platform: 16K MAC addresses, 4K ARP/NDP entries, 4K VLANs, static routes (894 IPv4 / 126 IPv6) plus RIP (32 IPv4), DHCP server (2K leases), sFlow, SNMP, console/telnet/SSH CLI and the AV web GUI. Ultra90 PoE++ 802.3bt PSEs, which the datasheet footnotes as backward compatible with 802.3af (15.4 W) and 802.3at (30 W) as well as 802.3bt at 60, 75 and 90 W. The model string carries the SKU because the catalogue key strips punctuation: M4250-10G2XF-PoE+ and M4250-10G2XF-PoE++ are the same box to modelKey(), and one identity cannot hold both variants. Sources: datasheet https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf and https://kb.netgear.com/000064904/NETGEAR-AV-Line-of-Fully-Managed-Switches-M4250-Series."
